{
  "dataset": "snag-quickchat-parser-corpus",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "status": "Shared corpus — proposed by the team, not an instructor requirement",
  "purpose": [
    "Snag ships TWO Quick Chat parsers: web-next/app/lib/parseQuick.ts (the one the UI",
    "actually calls) and finance.parse_quick_text (exposed at POST /quick). Both were",
    "tested, but never against each other — so a divergence outside the known D2/D4",
    "regressions would not be caught. Defect D2 was present in BOTH parsers, which is",
    "exactly why agreement has to be measured rather than assumed.",
    "",
    "This file is the single source of truth read by both suites:",
    "  web-next/app/lib/parseQuick.corpus.test.ts   (vitest)",
    "  evaluation/tests/test_w2c_parser_agreement.py (pytest)",
    "",
    "Only parser-intrinsic fields are compared. account_id / category_id are excluded",
    "on purpose: the TypeScript parser receives accounts and categories as arguments",
    "while the Python one reads them from the database, so an id mismatch would be a",
    "difference in inputs, not in parsing.",
    "",
    "`date` is relative to the reference date each suite pins, expressed as a day",
    "offset, so the corpus does not rot. null means 'no date mentioned' (both parsers",
    "must fall back to the reference date)."
  ],
  "fields_compared": ["kind", "amount", "note", "date_offset_days"],
  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-001",
      "input": "250 lunch",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 250.0,
      "note": "lunch",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["basic", "expense"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-002",
      "input": "1.2k groceries",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 1200.0,
      "note": "groceries",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["k_shorthand"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-003",
      "input": "2m bonus",
      "kind": "income",
      "amount": 2000000.0,
      "note": "bonus",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["m_shorthand", "income", "keyword"],
      "notes": "'bonus' is in the income keyword set of BOTH parsers, so this is income despite having no leading '+'. Verified identical: finance.py _INCOME_WORDS and parseQuick.ts INCOME_WORDS list the same words."
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-004",
      "input": "+5000 salary",
      "kind": "income",
      "amount": 5000.0,
      "note": "salary",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["income", "plus_prefix"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-005",
      "input": "300 dinner yesterday",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 300.0,
      "note": "dinner",
      "date_offset_days": -1,
      "tags": ["relative_date"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-006",
      "input": "150 coffee today",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 150.0,
      "note": "coffee",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["relative_date"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-007",
      "input": "500 rent tomorrow",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 500.0,
      "note": "rent",
      "date_offset_days": 1,
      "tags": ["relative_date"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-008",
      "input": "250 milk",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 250.0,
      "note": "milk",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["regression", "D4"],
      "notes": "D4: the amount suffix used to swallow the next word's first letter, giving 250,000,000 and a note of 'ilk'. Present in both parsers."
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-009",
      "input": "250 kilo rice",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 250.0,
      "note": "kilo rice",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["regression", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-010",
      "input": "80 kape",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 80.0,
      "note": "kape",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["regression", "D4", "filipino"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-011",
      "input": "300 movie tickets",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 300.0,
      "note": "movie tickets",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["regression", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-012",
      "input": "1,250.50 supplies",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 1250.5,
      "note": "supplies",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["thousands_separator", "decimals"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-013",
      "input": "transfer 2000 to savings",
      "kind": "transfer",
      "amount": 2000.0,
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["transfer"],
      "notes": "note text is not compared: the two parsers strip the transfer keyword differently, which is a cosmetic difference rather than a parse disagreement."
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-014",
      "input": "₱750 dinner",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 750.0,
      "note": "dinner",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["peso_sign"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-015",
      "input": "99 load",
      "kind": "expense",
      "amount": 99.0,
      "note": "load",
      "date_offset_days": 0,
      "tags": ["basic"]
    }
  ],
  "rejected_cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-R01",
      "input": "lunch with friends",
      "reason": "no amount",
      "tags": ["invalid"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-R02",
      "input": "",
      "reason": "empty input",
      "tags": ["invalid"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-R03",
      "input": "   ",
      "reason": "whitespace only",
      "tags": ["invalid"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "QCK-R04",
      "input": "0 nothing",
      "reason": "non-positive amount",
      "tags": ["invalid"]
    }
  ]
}
